Owner snag 2026-11-24, world issue I-068 (S-127, Papa John's w149814013, cell 50,-36): "no front window in level 2 (bay is probably too much)."

Cause (checked on the recorded 2026-11-24 plan, journal seq 2302; no dry run): the street end of Papa John's is a one-storey flat strip and the two-storey range rises behind it. The wall above the strip roof is a zone step inside the same building. shell_zoned (lib/builds/feature_build.py) makes it wall because a neighbour column's top is lower, but FacadePlanning.windows -> face_runs (lib/builds/feature_facade.py) keeps only cells where exposed() finds the neighbour outside the building's ownership, so a same-building step is never offered windows. The step wall is five columns on a stair-stepped diagonal facing N and W. 6516,-4569, 6517,-4570 and 6517,-4571 have only the strip (same building) on their lower sides, so face_runs never offers them. The end columns 6515,-4568 and 6518,-4572 also touch outside and are refused as corner piers. All are brick y36-38 under the y39 eave. The strip deck is y35 with carpet at y36. Row y37 holds 13 glass blocks elsewhere, none here. The shop band is not the cause (its top is at most y36). Not measured: how many other zoned specs have such walls.

Wanted: the window pass treats a zone-step wall face (neighbour in that direction is the same feature with a lower roof) as a window face for the rows above the lower neighbour's roof, with the same rules as an outside face (pier rhythm, facade_plan rows when given, choose_windows checks). Do not change exposed(): doors use it (feature_doors.py about lines 92 and 263) and so does house_build.py. Add a window-only step-face test used by windows() and passed to choose_windows, so the corner and tread rules see step faces. State whether the glazing-share report (face_run) counts step faces. The sill is the lower roof's top, carpet included. Plain windows only, no bays. Generic, keyed on geometry, no shop-specific code.

Files: lib/builds/feature_facade.py (windows, face_runs), lib/builds/window_openings.py (step face in choose_windows / outside_ground), colocated tests (lib/builds/test_feature_build.py or test_window_openings.py).

